smoothstep.doc:
Returns 0.0 if `x ≤ edge0` and 1.0 if `x ≥ edge1`, and performs smooth Hermite interpolation between 0 and 1 when `edge0 < x < edge1`.

This is useful in cases where you would want a threshold function with a smooth transition.

This is equivalent to:

```glsl
genFType t;
t = clamp ((x - edge0) / (edge1 - edge0), 0, 1);
return t * t * (3 - 2 * t);
```

(And similarly for doubles.) Results are undefined if `edge0 ≥ edge1`.

refract.doc:
For the incident vector `I` and surface normal `N`, and the ratio of indices of refraction `eta`, return the refraction vector. The result is computed by the refraction equation shown below.

```
k = 1.0 - eta * eta * (1.0 - \textbf{dot}(N,I) \cdot \textbf{dot}(N,I))
```

```
\begin{aligned}
result &=
  \begin{cases}
    genFType(0.0), & k < 0.0 \\
    eta * I - (eta * \textbf{dot}(N,I) + \sqrt { k }) * N, & \textbf{otherwise}
  \end{cases}
\end{aligned}
```

The input parameters for the incident vector `I` and the surface normal `N` must already be normalized to get the desired results.

